1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,050
Welcome to Green Vale Agricultural Park.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,746
As you know, we have only been open a week

3
00:00:05,746 --> 00:00:08,220
so you are amongst our first visitors.

4
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:14,094
We have lots of fascinating indoor and outdoor exhibits on our huge complex, spreading

5
00:00:14,094 --> 00:00:15,060
hundreds of hectares.

6
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:21,221
Our remit is to give educational opportunities to the wider public as well as

7
00:00:21,221 --> 00:00:26,780
to offer research sites for a wide variety of agriculturists and other scientists.

8
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:30,190
Let's start by seeing what there is to do.

9
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:36,293
As you can see here on our giant wall plan, we are now situated

10
00:00:36,293 --> 00:00:38,039
in the Reception block o..

11
00:00:38,039 --> 00:00:38,260
here.

12
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:42,651
As you walk out of the main door into the park there is a

13
00:00:42,651 --> 00:00:43,860
path you can follow.

14
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:49,060
If you follow this route you will immediately come into the Rare Breeds section,

15
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:53,035
where we keep a wide variety of animals which I shall be telling you

16
00:00:53,035 --> 00:00:54,220
a little more about later.

17
00:00:54,220 --> 00:01:01,000
Next to this.., moving east.., is the large grazing area for the rare breeds.

18
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,630
Then further east.., in the largest section of our Park is the Forest Area.

19
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:11,031
South of the grazing area and in fact just next to the Reception block

20
00:01:11,031 --> 00:01:12,780
is our Experimental Crop Area.

21
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:16,007
In the middle of the Park...

22
00:01:16,007 --> 00:01:24,245
this circular area is our lake These two small rectangular shapes here.., are the

23
00:01:24,245 --> 00:01:26,370
Fish Farms where we rear fish for sale.

24
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:31,775
To the east of those is the marsh area which attracts a great many

25
00:01:31,775 --> 00:01:32,820
migrant birds.

26
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:40,007
In the south-eastern corner, beyond the marsh, is our Market Garden area, growing vegetables

27
00:01:40,007 --> 00:01:40,910
and flowers.

28
00:01:40,910 --> 00:01:45,847
All these areas can be visited by the general public for almost all the

29
00:01:45,847 --> 00:01:46,210
year..,

30
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:47,596
although...

31
00:01:47,596 --> 00:01:52,618
please take note of the large signs at the entrance to each area which

32
00:01:52,618 --> 00:01:53,000
tell..,

33
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,316
which tell you when certain areas are being used for particular controlled experiments

34
00:01:58,316 --> 00:02:02,730
and are therefore temporarily out of bounds to the public.

35
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:07,630
You can see for yourself what a huge area the park covers

36
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:12,370
and a key question is always, how can we move around?

37
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:18,827
Well you have a choice of means.., all environmentally friendly.., cars are banned in

38
00:02:18,827 --> 00:02:19,330
the park.

39
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:25,130
We have bicycles which you can hire behind the Reception block.., here.., the healthy

40
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:29,986
ones of you can go on foot and finally there's our electric tram, powered

41
00:02:29,986 --> 00:02:31,050
from solar cells.

42
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:33,940
You find more information about this at the front entrance.

43
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:38,179
A good place to start on your tour is the Rare Breeds section.

44
00:02:38,179 --> 00:02:43,060
We keep goats, sheep and hens and other kinds of poultry.

45
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:46,151
We are also thinking of bringing in cows and horses

46
00:02:46,151 --> 00:02:49,860
but we do not, as yet, have facilities for these bigger animals.

47
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:56,906
The animals are fed in public twice a day and a short lecture given on their feeding habits

48
00:02:56,906 --> 00:02:58,080
and nutritional needs.

49
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:02,006
These are very popular with the public but of course we mustn't lose sight

50
00:03:02,006 --> 00:03:04,250
of the main purpose of having this section,

51
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:10,245
not as such to preserve rare animals but to maintain the diversity of breeds

52
00:03:10,245 --> 00:03:13,670
to broaden the gene pool for agricultural development.

53
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:19,008
Green Vale changes with the seasons with different events happening at different times of

54
00:03:19,008 --> 00:03:19,770
the year.

55
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:25,311
May will be perhaps our most spectacular month with the arrival of the Canada geese

56
00:03:25,311 --> 00:03:29,005
and when our fruit trees will be in full blossom,

57
00:03:29,005 --> 00:03:32,330
but there are interesting events on all year round..,

58
00:03:32,330 --> 00:03:38,471
for example John Havers, our expert fly fisherman is currently giving displays on the

59
00:03:38,471 --> 00:03:38,910
lake.

60
00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:44,689
Each of the sections has its own seasonal calendar.., please consult the summary board

61
00:03:44,689 --> 00:03:46,340
at the main entrance.

62
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:51,330
And the final section, as we return to the Reception blocks, is the orchard.

63
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:55,629
Do take time to browse round our shop.., there is a wide selection of

64
00:03:55,629 --> 00:03:58,700
books on wildlife, some of them written by local authors,

65
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:04,041
and the history of farming, including organic farming, something which the park will be

66
00:04:04,041 --> 00:04:06,330
diversifying into in the coming months.
